  "term": "anterior cingulate cortex",
  "definition": "The anterior cingulate cortex is the front part of the cingulate cortex on the inner surface of the frontal lobe, next to the corpus callosum. It is involved in decision-making and in regulating emotions and body processes such as heart rate and blood pressure.",
